WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.532
A typical Open WebUI deployment includes a browser client, the Open WebUI application, backend database and configuration storage, one or more model runtimes or inference APIs, logs, uploaded files, user accounts, and sometimes a reverse proxy.

00:00:16.532 --> 00:00:19.242
The browser is where the user interacts.

00:00:19.242 --> 00:00:21.816
The application manages the workspace.

00:00:21.816 --> 00:00:24.323
The model backend performs inference.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:28.727
Each layer has its own operational and security responsibilities.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:32.115
Prompts and responses move through several places.

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:34.689
A user writes a prompt in the browser.

00:00:34.689 --> 00:00:42.955
The application may add system instructions, conversation history, selected model settings, or retrieved document context.

00:00:42.955 --> 00:00:46.749
The request is then sent to a configured model endpoint.

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:55.286
The response returns through the application and is displayed to the user, often with conversation state stored for later use.

00:00:55.286 --> 00:01:05.313
Storage matters because Open WebUI can preserve configuration, users, conversations, uploaded content, knowledge collections, and application state.

00:01:05.313 --> 00:01:08.430
Logs may capture operational events or errors.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.411
Backups may preserve the database and files.

00:01:11.411 --> 00:01:15.544
If storage is ephemeral, upgrades or restarts can lose state.

00:01:15.544 --> 00:01:24.081
If storage is persistent, it must be protected because it may contain sensitive prompts, outputs, files, and endpoint details.

00:01:24.081 --> 00:01:28.959
Architecture clarity helps operators troubleshoot and secure the system.

00:01:28.959 --> 00:01:41.696
They should know where accounts are stored, how model endpoints are configured, where files live, what data is logged, what is backed up, and whether access is local, LAN-based, or remote.

00:01:41.696 --> 00:01:47.726
A clean mental model prevents the interface from hiding important infrastructure choices.
